{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q82949971","formula":"C₁₂H₁₇NO₂","hill":"C12H17NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":12.0,"H":17.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"4,7-Dimethoxy-5-methyl-2,3-dihydro-1H-inden-2-amine"},"descriptions":{"en":"DOM-AI, also known as 4,7-dimethoxy-5-methyl-2-aminoindane, is a putative serotonergic psychedelic of the 2-aminoindane family related to DOM. It is a cyclized phenethylamine and the cyclized 2-aminoindane analogue of DOM. The drug fully substituted for LSD in rodent drug discrimination tests, suggesting that it may have hallucinogenic effects in humans. However, DOM-AI was much less potent than DOM in these tests, with an ED50Tooltip median effective dose of 2.18 mg/kg, which was approximately 1/15th that of DOM. Nonetheless, DOM-AI is still active in showing psychedelic-like effects in animals, in contrast to its analogues DOM-AT and DOM-CR."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":3016787,"mass":207.27,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=CC(=C2CC(CC2=C1OC)N)OC","inchikey":"LBSOVXNUJAVVNS-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"4,7-dimethoxy-5-methyl-2,3-dihydro-1H-inden-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3016787","atoms":32,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.349,"y":1.402,"z":0.448,"el":"O"},{"x":1.441,"y":-2.522,"z":-0.546,"el":"O"},{"x":2.943,"y":2.753,"z":-0.094,"el":"N"},{"x":2.026,"y":1.736,"z":0.397,"el":"C"},{"x":0.55,"y":2.112,"z":0.155,"el":"C"},{"x":2.242,"y":0.371,"z":-0.287,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.082,"y":0.756,"z":0.1,"el":"C"},{"x":0.878,"y":-0.232,"z":-0.151,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.423,"y":0.434,"z":0.219,"el":"C"},{"x":0.517,"y":-1.562,"z":-0.287,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.795,"y":-0.906,"z":0.096,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.832,"y":-1.897,"z":-0.156,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.229,"y":-1.309,"z":0.223,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.941,"y":2.02,"z":-0.696,"el":"C"},{"x":2.05